# Keep every checkout byte-identical to what is committed.
#
# Roslyn embeds a source-content checksum in the assembly's debug directory and
# portable PDB, so the same source compiled with different line endings produces
# a different dist/Ramblers.dll. Without this file that depended on each
# developer's core.autocrlf, which made the SHA-256 that build.ps1 prints
# incomparable between machines and left the committed artifact unreproducible.
#
# LF is chosen over CRLF so the working tree matches the stored blob exactly:
# the bytes that are committed are the bytes the compiler reads.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never line-ending convert build output.
*.dll binary
*.pdb binary
*.exe binary
